    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21861" root="شحن" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَشْحُونٌ</span></b>  A ship (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلْكٌ</span>, so in the Kur [xxvi.
119 &amp;c.], S, L, or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْكَبٌ</span>, K [in the L, erroneously, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَكَبٌ</span>],) <i>Filled</i> [or <i>laded, and completely
equipped</i> or <i>furnished:</i> see 1, first sentence];
(S, L, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَاحِنٌ</span></b> , like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَاتِمٌ</span> in the sense
of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُكْتُومٌ</span>, (L, K,) mentioned by Kr. (L.)

